      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{628bc9aba732aa0b6efc0464|full_name}: Safety settings are built around Trust ranks, and have been a great use for self-moderation for the past five years.\n\nI at least think that groups should implement optional rank filtering, if they so care. Nuisance users can still join my group instances, and there is nothing that I can do to prevent that. \n\nBanishing a user can sometimes result in an attempt at retaliation via a recently-created Visitor rank account in attempt to harass group users and moderators to evade the ban. So, I think Trust filters would be good.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
