  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-18T13:42:44.682Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The prospect of the amount of difficult people joining with the new android vrchat client is horrible. But it's also a good decision for VRCHAT. It will add tons of people to the platform and VR itself. \n\nBut VRCHAT really needs to implement better tools to keep these people away too. VRC already has a horrible reputation. Every single person from the news just writes how horrible the rooms are. Just screaming children everywhere. It also deters tons of serious people that would stay long term from the platform. This can cause a slow death because there are lots of new people, but none that stay.\n\nOne way would be to give instance creators the tools to exclude better. Being able to require different trust levels for different platforms. \n\nThis should be the standard for PCVR public instance creation:\n\nAndroid: Only trusted people\n\nQuest: Only known users and up\n\nDesktop: User and up\n\nPCVR: Visitor and up\n\nIt would make the game so much more peaceful.\n\nThe instances with these requirements fulfilled should also show at the top of the list of instances for PCVR users.\n\nUnfortunately blocking and muting from higher trust levels should count heavier towards downgrades in trust. Some automated tools would be important too. Were there high noise levels for a while from the user blocked? If yes, it should impact trust level much more. Both voice and avatar sounds need to count.\n\nIf VRCHAT is not careful, it could toxify the game culture a lot. And I'm sure online game creators would agree that this is very important.\n\nProbably suggest the news and press to use PC connected VR for the full experience too ;)",
